+    <section class="journal" aria-labelledby="journal-title">
+      <h2 id="journal-title">Roaster's Journal</h2>
+      <div id="journal-text">
+        <p>Every bag we roast begins months before it reaches our shop, usually with a long conversation over a
+          crackling video call with a farmer we have come to think of as a friend. We buy almost exclusively from small
+          family-owned farms and cooperatives in Ethiopia, Colombia, Guatemala, and Sumatra, and we try to visit each
+          one at least once every two years. Walking the rows, tasting cherries straight off the branch, and watching
+          the wet mill at work tells us more about a harvest than any spec sheet ever could.</p>
+        <p>When samples arrive, we roast them in tiny batches and cup them blind, scoring each on aroma, acidity, body,
+          sweetness, and finish. Only a small fraction make the cut. We are looking for clarity and character, but also
+          for traceability: we want to know the farm, the altitude, the variety, and the processing method behind every
+          lot. If a supplier cannot tell us those things, we move on.</p>
+        <p>Price matters as much as flavor. We pay well above the commodity "C" market price and agree on it before
+          the harvest, so farmers can plan their season, pay pickers fairly, and invest in better drying beds and
+          fermentation tanks. Many of our partners have used these long-term contracts to fund schools, clean-water
+          projects, and replanting of aging trees with more climate-resilient varieties.</p>
+        <p>Once green coffee lands at our roastery, it rests for a few weeks before we profile-roast it. We log every
+          batch, taste it again after a few days of degassing, and adjust. Coffee is a seasonal crop, so our menu
+          changes as harvests do. When a favorite lot sells out, we would rather say goodbye than serve something
+          past its prime, and we will happily tell you the story of whatever replaces it.</p>
+      </div>
+      <button type="button" id="summarize-btn" class="btn">Summarize</button>
+      <p id="summarize-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
+      <ul id="summary-list" aria-label="Summary"></ul>
+    </section>
